  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nHigh pressure aloft will strengthen into the weekend with periods\nof weak easterly offshore flow during the weekend. Not much\nchange is expected in high temperatures on Friday for the\nmountains and deserts while the coast and valleys warm 4 to 8\ndegrees. High temperatures on Friday for the coast and valleys\nwill range from the 80s near the coast to the upper 90s to 105 \nfor the Inland Empire with Moderate to locally Major HeatRisk for \nthe coast and valleys.\n\nNot much change in high temperatures is expected for mountains and\ndeserts for the weekend while coastal areas warm another 5 degrees\non Saturday with only slight additional warming on Sunday. Low\ntemperatures for coastal areas will warm from around 70 on\nSaturday to the lower to mid 70s on Sunday. Widespread Major \nHeatRisk is expected on Saturday for the coast into the western \nvalleys with Major to isolated Extreme HeatRisk on Sunday.\n\nHigh temperatures for the weekend will range from around 5 degrees\nabove average for the lower deserts to as much as 15 to 20 degrees\nabove average for coastal areas into the western valleys. High\ntemperatures for the weekend will range from the mid 80s to around\n90 near the coast to the mid 90s to 105 for the valleys with the\nlower deserts around 100.\n\nThere could be periods of gusty east winds during the weekend for\nthe coastal slopes of the mountains into the inland valleys with \ngusts to 25 to 35 mph.\n\nA long-duration heat wave, especially for the coast and valleys,\nis likely to persist for much of next week into the following\nweekend.",
